{"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/Group-swift.struct"],"title":"Structures","generated":true,"anchor":"Structures"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/init(id:group:swing:offset:tempo:dynamics:isDaCapo:segno:dalsegno:coda:tocoda:divisions:impliesForwardRepeat:fine:timeOnly:isPizzicato:pan:elevation:damperPedal:softPedal:sostenutoPedal:)"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/coda","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/dalsegno","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/damperPedal","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/divisions","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/dynamics","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/elevation","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/fine","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/group-swift.property","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/id","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/impliesForwardRepeat","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/isDaCapo","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/isPizzicato","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/offset","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/pan","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/segno","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/softPedal","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/sostenutoPedal","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/swing","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/tempo","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/timeOnly","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/tocoda"],"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/Equatable-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSound"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Tempo is expressed in quarter notes per minute. If 0, the sound-generating program should prompt the user at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the time of compiling a sound (MIDI) file.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Dynamics (or MIDI velocity) are expressed as a percentage of the default forte value (90 for MIDI 1.0).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Dacapo indicates to go back to the beginning of the movement. When used it always has the value “yes”."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Segno and dalsegno are used for backwards jumps to a segno sign; coda and tocoda are used for forward jumps to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a coda sign. If there are multiple jumps, the value of these parameters can be used to name and distinguish"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them. If segno or coda is used, the divisions attribute can also be used to indicate the number of divisions"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per quarter note. Otherwise sound and MIDI generating programs may have to recompute this."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"By default, a dalsegno or dacapo attribute indicates that the jump should occur the first time through, while"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a tocoda attribute indicates the jump should occur the second time through. The time that jumps occur can be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"changed by using the time-only attribute."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The forward-repeat attribute indicates that a forward repeat sign is implied but not displayed. It is used for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"example in two-part forms with repeats, such as a minuet and trio where no repeat is displayed at the start of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the trio. This usually occurs after a barline. When used it always has the value of “yes”."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The fine attribute follows the final note or rest in a movement with a da capo or dal segno direction. If"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"numeric, the value represents the actual duration of the final note or rest, which can be ambiguous in written"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"notation and different among parts and voices. The value may also be “yes” to indicate no change to the final"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"duration."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the sound element applies only particular times through a repeat, the time-only attribute indicates which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"times to apply the sound element."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pizzicato in a sound element effects all following notes. Yes indicates pizzicato, no indicates arco."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The pan and elevation attributes are deprecated in Version 2.0. The pan and elevation elements in the midi-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instrument element should be used instead. The meaning of the pan and elevation attributes is the same as for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the pan and elevation elements. If both are present, the mid-instrument elements take priority."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The damper-pedal, soft-pedal, and sostenuto-pedal attributes effect playback of the three common piano pedals"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and their MIDI controller equivalents. The yes value indicates the pedal is depressed; no indicates the pedal"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is released. A numeric value from 0 to 100 may also be used for half pedaling. This value is the percentage"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that the pedal is depressed. A value of 0 is equivalent to no, and a value of 100 is equivalent to yes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Instrument changes, MIDI devices, MIDI instruments, and playback techniques are changed using the instrument-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change, midi-device, midi-instrument, and play elements. When there are multiple instances of these elements,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they should be grouped together by instrument using the id attribute values."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The offset element is used to indicate that the sound takes place offset from the current score position. If"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the sound element is a child of a direction element, the sound offset element overrides the direction offset"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element if both elements are present. Note that the offset reflects the intended musical position for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change in sound. It should not be used to compensate for latency issues in particular hardware configurations."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps the MusicXML "},{"code":"<sound>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}]}]}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","title":"MXLSound","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLSoundV","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSound"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSound"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Music","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMusicItem","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLRest","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPitch","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Music"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The sound element contains general playback parameters. They can stand alone within a part\/measure, or be a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component element within a direction."}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/timeOnly":{"title":"timeOnly","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Indicates which times through a repeat this sound element applies to, if only particular times."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound\/timeonly","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/timeOnly","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"timeOnly"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLTimeOnly","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLTimeOnlya"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/SQ":{"title":"Swift.Equatable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/swing":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound\/swing","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Specifies playback as swung rather than even notes."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/swing","title":"swing","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"swing","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLSwing","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLSwingV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAttributes":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLAttributes","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLAttributes","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLAttributes","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlattributes","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The attributes element contains musical information that typically changes on measure boundaries. This","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"includes key and time signatures, clefs, transpositions, and staving. When attributes are changed mid-measure,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it affects the music in score order, not in MusicXML document order.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/pan":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"pan"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLRotationDegreesa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLRotationDegrees"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"pan","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/pan","abstract":[{"text":"Deprecated in favor of the pan element in midi-instrument. Specifies placement of sound in a 3-D space","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"relative to the listener, in degrees.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound\/pan"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLDirection","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A direction is a musical indication that is not necessarily attached to a specific note. Two or more may be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"combined to indicate words followed by the start of a dashed line, the end of a wedge followed by dynamics,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"etc. For applications where a specific direction is indeed attached to a specific note, the direction element","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can be associated with the first note element that follows it in score order that is not in a different voice.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLDirection","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLDirection"},"doc://IvorMXL/SH":{"title":"Swift.Hashable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/Equatable-Implementations":{"title":"Equatable Implementations","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound\/equatable-implementations","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/Equatable-Implementations","type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","abstract":[]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/isPizzicato":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/isPizzicato","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Boolean value indicating whether following notes are played pizzicato ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":") or arco ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isPizzicato","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound\/ispizzicato","title":"isPizzicato","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/s8SendableP":{"title":"Swift.Sendable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote":{"title":"MXLNote","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNote"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Notes are the most common type of MusicXML data. The MusicXML format distinguishes between elements used for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sound information and elements used for notation information (e.g., tie is used for sound, tied for notation)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Thus grace notes do not have a duration element. Cue notes have a duration element, as do forward elements,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but no tie elements. Having these two types of information available can make interchange easier, as some"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"programs handle one type of information more readily than the other."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNote"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/softPedal":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Controls playback of the soft pedal. A numeric value from 0 to 100 may be used for half pedaling."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound\/softpedal","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/softPedal","title":"softPedal","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"softPedal"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLYesNoNumberO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLYesNoNumber"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMusicItem":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmusicitem","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMusicItem","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMusicItem"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"One of the alternatives for a music item."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMusicItem"}],"title":"MXLMusicItem"},"doc://IvorMXL/s8CopyableP":{"title":"Swift.Copyable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPitch":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLPitch","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPitch","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLPitch","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpitch","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"